Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer* position with Apple's Media Services Everywhere team. I bring more than three years of experience architecting shared frameworks, APIs, intuitive interfaces, and business-critical features, supported by an MS in Computer Science from Pace University. The opportunity to build foundations that enable teams across Apple to deliver exceptional customer experiences directly matches the platform and integration work reflected throughout my resume.

At Sperse, I architected *TypeScript*, *Kotlin*, and *Swift shared UI frameworks* for features spanning mobile, desktop, Smart TVs, and game consoles. I also designed and implemented *low-level networking and authentication APIs* in C++, FastAPI, and FastMCP, exposing 160+ secure backend actions through validated contracts, access control, and production monitoring. Working with cross-functional teams on integration and adoption, I translated product and design requirements into features serving 10,000+ users. I reinforced that delivery discipline by building tests and writing documentation across unit tests, integration tests, API contracts, adoption guides, CI/CD, and OpenTelemetry evaluations.

At Qualitest, I designed cross-platform Java, Kotlin, and C++ APIs for storage operations and authentication through expiring signed URLs across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I also built business-critical features with AWS Step Functions and Lambda across 100K+ weekly executions, adding automated tests, failure recovery, and operational documentation. Partnering with design and business stakeholders on React interfaces and PostgreSQL APIs strengthened my ability to craft intuitive experiences and drive framework integration and adoption.

Apple's commitment to cross-functional collaboration in service of an *extraordinary user experience* strongly resonates with how I build software. I am equally drawn to Apple's focus on creating powerful tools that empower others, with privacy and accessibility treated as core design values. I would welcome the opportunity to bring strong programming fundamentals, quality and attention to detail, and the aptitude to independently learn new languages and frameworks to the Everywhere team as it shapes how millions of customers discover, subscribe to, and engage with Apple's services ecosystem. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your consideration.

